JET_CLI_EFFECT_SOURCE: "// The machine effects are written here, not in Rust.\n//\n// This is ordinary Jet source. Each type implements `Effect`: a struct is an\n// effect root with no members, and an enum is a closed family whose cases are\n// its leaves (`FS.Read`). These are what the machine does; Core declares the\n// services built on them (DB, Log, Secret) in Core/Effects/Effects.jet, each\n// with a `#FX(…)` line naming the machine effects it may use, and the Prelude\n// exports both. Effect parsing, marker arguments (`#FX(Net, FS)`), fact\n// registration, manifest and `--allow`/`--deny` validation, diagnostics, and\n// reflection all read the two lists (Foundation's generated\n// Registry/EffectVocabulary.jet carries them to the compiler), so an effect\n// exists exactly when it is written in one of them. The order here, then\n// Core's, is the canonical order of a written effect row.\n// `irreversible: fn(self) -> Bool` says which effects a `#Transact` rollback\n// can't take back; a family is irreversible when any of its cases is.\n// `Panic`, `Mem` and `Time.Wait` are deny-only: a policy may refuse them but\n// never has to grant them.\n\nNet: struct {{\n    impl Effect {{\n        irreversible: fn(self) -> Bool {{ true }}\n    }}\n}}\n\nFS: enum {{\n    Read\n    Write\n\n    impl Effect {{\n        irreversible: fn(self) -> Bool {{ self == .Write }}\n    }}\n}}\n\nIO: struct {{\n    impl Effect {{}}\n}}\n\nTime: enum {{\n    Wait\n\n    impl Effect {{}}\n}}\n\nRand: enum {{\n    Draw\n\n    impl Effect {{}}\n}}\n\nEnv: struct {{\n    impl Effect {{}}\n}}\n\nExec: enum {{\n    Exit\n    Args\n\n    impl Effect {{\n        irreversible: fn(self) -> Bool {{ true }}\n    }}\n}}\n\nGPU: struct {{\n    impl Effect {{}}\n}}\n\n// The foreign languages: a call into one has that language's leaf. This is\n// the one foreign-language list; Tools/agent/CoreSourceRows.jet writes the\n// `#FFI(<lang>)` language menu (Core/Compiler/Lang.jet) and the binder\n// languages (Jetpack's ForeignLanguage) from these cases.\nFFI: enum {{\n    Go\n    Java\n    DotNet\n    Fortran\n    Cobol\n    Tcl\n    Lua\n    Ada\n    Pascal\n    Dart\n    PowerShell\n    Perl\n    Ruby\n    Php\n    R\n    Com\n    C\n    Cpp\n    Asm\n    Py\n    Octave\n    Rust\n    JS\n    Swift\n\n    impl Effect {{\n        irreversible: fn(self) -> Bool {{ true }}\n    }}\n}}\n\nBrowser: struct {{\n    impl Effect {{}}\n}}\n\nPanic: struct {{\n    impl Effect {{}}\n}}\n\nMem: enum {{\n    Alloc\n    Rc\n\n    impl Effect {{}}\n}}\n\n// Core's service effects: what Core builds on the machine effects of\n// Compiler/Prelude/Effects.jet, declared the way a package declares a library\n// effect. The `#FX(…)` above each lists the machine effects a row naming it\n// may use; a denial still checks what each call really reaches, so `!Net`\n// catches a database driver that talks to a server and passes a local file.\n// The Prelude exports these with the machine effects, so rows name them bare\n// (`-[DB.Read]>`, `!Log`). The form is that of Effects.jet, and\n// Tools/agent/CoreSourceRows.jet reads both into the compiler.\n\n#FX(Net, FS)\nDB: enum {{\n    Read\n    Write\n\n    impl Effect {{}}\n}}\n\n#FX(IO, FS, Net)\nLog: struct {{\n    impl Effect {{}}\n}}\n\n#FX(Env, FS, Net)\nSecret: struct {{\n    impl Effect {{}}\n}}\n\n// The metaprogramming effects: the compiler operations library code running\n// inside the compiler may perform. Reading the program needs no Meta effect,\n// so a read-only lint's row is `-[]>`; a marker or derive that writes checked\n// declarations is `-[Meta.Generate]>`, and replacing a declaration's body is\n// `Meta.Rewrite`. Adding a type from text checks `Generate`, `Types` and `Raw`\n// together. The bare `#FX` lists no machine effect: host work keeps its own\n// machine effects and gates.\n// The form is that of Compiler/Prelude/Effects.jet, and\n// Tools/agent/CoreSourceRows.jet reads it into the compiler after\n// Core/Effects/Effects.jet.\n#FX\nMeta: enum {{\n    Generate\n    Include\n    Rewrite\n    Types\n    Raw\n\n    impl Effect {{}}\n}}\n"

